<title>JAPAN: BOJ says undecided on additional help for 'jusen'.</title>
<headline>BOJ says undecided on additional help for 'jusen'.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Japan Governor Yasuo Matsushita said on Wednesday that the central bank would decide whether to give additional funds to a government plan to wind up failed mortgage firms after private institutions come up with a consensus on their own contributions.</p>
<p>Private financial institutions are currently considering setting up a special fund worth 800 billion yen, then giving the profits from investing the money to the scheme to wind up the mortgage firms, known as &quot;jusen&quot;.</p>
</text>
